+| `pkg/server/server.go` | Added `moduleManager` field, shutdown integration |
+
+### 6.3 Test Results
+
+- **22 new tests** — all passing
+- **All existing tests** — continue to pass unchanged
+- **Full binary** — compiles successfully
+- **All packages** (`go build ./...`) — compile successfully
+
+---
+
+## 7. Future Enhancements
+
+1. **Build tags for slim binaries**: Use `//go:build !slim` tags to exclude provider code from the core binary at compile time, enabling truly smaller core binaries.
+
+2. **Module health checks**: Add a `Health()` method to the Module interface so the module manager can detect and restart unhealthy modules.
+
+3. **Module dependency graph**: Allow modules to declare dependencies on other modules, enabling proper load/unload ordering.
+
+4. **Hot module reload**: Support reloading an updated `.so` file without restarting traefik.
+
+5. **Module API endpoint**: Expose `/api/modules` in the API for runtime module status inspection (the `ModuleStatusHandler` is already implemented).
+
+6. **WASM modules**: Extend the loader to support WebAssembly modules alongside Go plugins, for cross-platform module distribution.
